cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CERM in research, please cite this software."
title: "CERM"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Kawahara"
    given-names: "Taishi"
version: "1.0.0a1"
license: "Apache-2.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Tk-visionary/CERM"
url: "https://github.com/Tk-visionary/CERM"
abstract: >-
  CERM is an experimental compiler-aware finite-state learner for tabular
  classification and regression, with auditable semantic programs, independent
  multi-output bundles, and separate training and inference optimizations.
keywords:
  - tabular machine learning
  - classification
  - regression
  - multilabel classification
  - finite-state models
  - model compilation
  - scikit-learn
